Original commit body from ee6f89892a1a7860fcff52027d0cf970c35c5720:

When the Structure tree is built from a behavior map (the normal case,
INV-jumim), the map names only files that yielded a symbol, so item counts
and the LOC column leave out data files and scripts no analyzer
recognises. On hypergumbo itself that was 132 tracked files, 394k lines
(mostly the vendored grammars' generated parser.c). One sentence under
the tree now says so, with JSON data and extensionless scripts as the
examples. Owner chose this disclosure over recording the survey's full
discovered-file list. ADR-0005 and spec updated.

